//! Help for querying, editing and comparing a program without external documentation.
pub fn summary() -> &'static str { "\nStructural command help:\n  lkjscript query --help    Question kinds, identities, text and continuations\n  lkjscript edit --help     Complete JSON request schema and operation examples\n  lkjscript compare --help  Checked comparison and separate source roots\n" }
pub fn topic(command: &str) -> &'static str {
    match command {
        "query" => "lkjscript query SOURCE [source/library/store options] [question options]\n\nAsk about an authenticated build snapshot. Keep the same SOURCE, --source-dir,\n--library-dir, --store and --store-key selectors used to publish that snapshot.\nSOURCE selects the program; --id selects a declaration inside it.\n\nFirst publish a snapshot:\n  lkjscript build src/main.lkj --source-dir ROOT --library-dir LIB \\\n    --index --store STORE --store-key KEY -o IMAGE\nCreate STORE first. KEY is a private 32-byte file outside source/library roots.\nThe build prints LKJSCRIPT_SNAPSHOT SNAPSHOT source=SOURCE_DIGEST checked-ir=IR_DIGEST.\n\nFind an identity and read its source:\n  lkjscript query src/main.lkj [same selectors] --snapshot SNAPSHOT \\\n    --kind outline --id crate --depth 2 --limit 40 --bytes 16384\n  lkjscript query src/main.lkj [same selectors] --snapshot SNAPSHOT \\\n    --kind text --id math::increment --limit 40 --bytes 16384\n\nCopy the quoted identity from a returned fact. The root is crate. Declaration\nidentities have no leading crate:: and are not file paths. Nested modules appear\nin the identity; copy an implementation's displayed identity exactly. For a\nparameter use its returned ::param:NAME identity. Body-local identities contain\na body epoch and must be queried again after a token-changing body edit.\n\nQuestion kinds:\n  outline     Child declarations and signatures; --depth follows descendants.\n  signature   One declaration's signature.\n  meta        Identity, origin, source location and source-text digest.\n  text        Exact authored item text, returned in bounded fragments.\n  item        Metadata and exact authored item text.\n  slice       Metadata/text plus directly mentioned signatures.\n  references  Recorded source-reference claims.\n  uses        Items this source declaration mentions.\n  callers     Checked callers of a demanded instance.\n  callees     Checked callees of a demanded instance.\n  impls       Recorded implementations.\n  instances   Demanded checked instances associated with a declaration.\n  type        Recorded type facts.\n  layout      Checked type layout facts.\n  authority   Reachable checked-IR effects.\n  dependents  Recorded dependent items.\n\n--depth, --limit and --bytes must be positive. Defaults: 1, 30 and 16384.\nThe complete reply, including its continuation, must fit --bytes. If the reply\nhas a cursor, repeat the same kind/id/depth/snapshot with --cursor HEX. Follow\ncontinuations before treating text or an outline as complete. Increase --bytes\nwhen even one complete reply cannot fit; a bound refusal writes no partial stdout.\n\nFacts distinguish source-claim from checked-ir. Missing recorded references do\nnot prove that no use exists. Generated declarations say source-projection=false;\nquery their defining declaration when an edit is needed. A query authenticates\nits historical producing compiler and does not check current source freshness.\nAfter an edit, build --index again to ask about the newly published source.\n\nA function's outline lists the IDs of its authored call sites; to replace one\ncall, see lkjscript edit --help (replace-call).\n\nTo change a returned function or declaration, run lkjscript edit --help.\n",
        "edit" => "lkjscript edit SOURCE --request REQUEST.json [source/library/store options]\n               [--dry-run]\nlkjscript edit SOURCE --against DESIRED_SOURCE [--against-source-dir ROOT]\n               [--against-library-dir LIB] [source/library/store options]\nlkjscript edit SOURCE --recover --store-key KEY [source/library options]\n\nUse a relative SOURCE when --source-dir selects its root. Applying or recovering\nneeds a private 32-byte --store-key file outside every source/library root.\n--dry-run checks a complete candidate and reports the plan without publishing.\nA normal request checks and atomically publishes all affected source files.\n\nA complete request file is JSON:\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"operations\": [\n    {\"op\": \"replace-body\", \"id\": \"math::increment\", \"source\": \"{ value + 2 }\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nversion must be the integer 1. operations is a nonempty array. Every operation\nneeds string fields op and id. The optional request field snapshot is the\nSOURCE_DIGEST printed as source= by query/build, not the immutable query SNAPSHOT.\nAn optional operation field expect is that item's source-text digest from meta.\nUnknown request fields, stale expected text and overlapping edits refuse.\n\nFind IDs with query --kind outline; obtain full source with --kind text or item.\nCopy the complete identity, including nested modules or an implementation owner.\nThe root is crate; declaration IDs have no leading crate:: and are not file paths.\nAll operations in one request address the same original snapshot. Put related\nchanges in one array so the complete candidate can be checked together.\n\nBasic operation objects (put one or more inside operations):\n  Replace a function's complete braced body:\n    {\"op\":\"replace-body\",\"id\":\"math::increment\",\"source\":\"{ value + 2 }\"}\n  Replace one authored call or method call with one expression:\n    {\"op\":\"replace-call\",\"id\":\"main::body:BODY_DIGEST::call:0\",\n     \"source\":\"value + 2\"}\n  Replace one complete authored declaration, including its signature/header:\n    {\"op\":\"replace-item\",\"id\":\"math::increment\",\n     \"source\":\"pub fn increment(value: i64) -> i64 { value + 2 }\"}\n  Add one complete item to a module:\n    {\"op\":\"add-item\",\"id\":\"math\",\"source\":\"pub fn twice(x: i64) -> i64 { x * 2 }\"}\n  Insert before an existing child instead of at the module end:\n    {\"op\":\"add-item\",\"id\":\"math\",\"before\":\"math::increment\",\n     \"source\":\"pub fn zero() -> i64 { 0 }\"}\n  Remove an item:\n    {\"op\":\"remove-item\",\"id\":\"math::unused\"}\n  Rename a resolved declaration and its proved uses:\n    {\"op\":\"rename\",\"id\":\"math::increment\",\"name\":\"advance\"}\n  Move a supported function or inline module:\n    {\"op\":\"move\",\"id\":\"math::helper\",\"parent\":\"other_module\"}\n\nreplace-body takes braces, not a fn declaration. replace-item takes exactly one\nwhole item and can replace an authored struct, enum or impl. add-item accepts a\nmodule parent; use replace-item for an existing impl when adding its member.\nSource is parsed in the item's real scope and independently checked before any\nfile is published. A rename/move additionally proves its supported preservation\ncontract. Generated declarations must be changed through their defining source.\n\nreplace-call changes one call site, not the function that contains it.\nFind call-site IDs with lkjscript query --kind outline --id FUNCTION --depth 1.\nRun lkjscript query --kind item on a call-site ID to read the call's exact text\nand its digest (--kind meta gives the digest and location only); pass that\ndigest as expect to make the edit refuse if the call has changed.\nA call-site ID includes its function's body digest: after a body edit that\nchanges tokens (not only whitespace or comments), query again for fresh IDs.\nThe source is wrapped in parentheses and newlines, so operator precedence and a\ntrailing line comment cannot change the surrounding code. It is then expanded\nand checked in the scope where the call is written.\nCalls produced by generated code are refused; edit the declaration that\ngenerates them. Calls whose authored text is not one complete expression are\nrefused too; use replace-body on the containing function instead.\n\nCreate one external module beneath an existing semantic and physical parent:\n{\"version\":1,\"operations\":[\n  {\"op\":\"add-item\",\"id\":\"crate\",\"source\":\"pub mod added;\",\n   \"projection\":{\"path\":\"src/added.lkj\",\"source\":\"pub fn value() -> i64 { 42 }\"}}\n]}\nprojection.path is relative to --source-dir and must be the loader's actual\nchild.lkj or child/mod.lkj candidate. Its parent directory must already exist.\nAn occupied alternate candidate refuses. This does not create directories or\nremove files; an absent file and an existing empty file are distinct.\n\nRefactor operation objects:\n  Reorder/retain parameters by their returned IDs; a descriptor adds one:\n    {\"op\":\"change-signature\",\"id\":\"math::combine\",\n     \"parameters\":[\"math::combine::param:right\",\"math::combine::param:left\",\n                   {\"name\":\"bias\",\"type\":\"i64\",\"argument\":\"current_bias\"}]}\n  Add a named field and supply the value for affected constructors:\n    {\"op\":\"add-field\",\"id\":\"Point\",\"source\":\"tag: i64\",\"value\":\"default_tag()\"}\n  Remove a field and supply the expression for affected accesses:\n    {\"op\":\"remove-field\",\"id\":\"Point::field:tag\",\"replacement\":\"fallback_tag()\"}\n  Add a variant and the arm for affected matches:\n    {\"op\":\"add-variant\",\"id\":\"Choice\",\"source\":\"Later(i64)\",\n     \"arm\":\"Choice::Later(_) => 0i64\"}\n  Remove a variant and replace its construction:\n    {\"op\":\"remove-variant\",\"id\":\"Choice::variant:Later\",\n     \"replacement\":\"Choice::Ready\"}\n  Inline a concrete free function; remove defaults to false:\n    {\"op\":\"inline-function\",\"id\":\"math::add\",\"remove\":true}\n    Optional sites is a nonempty array of exact returned call-site IDs.\n  Extract the expression selected by a returned call-site ID:\n    {\"op\":\"extract-function\",\"id\":\"main::body:BODY_DIGEST::call:0\",\n     \"name\":\"calculate\",\"parameters\":[],\"result\":\"i64\"}\n    Captures use descriptors with id, name, type and argument.\n    For another expression, id selects its function and expect is mandatory;\n    start/end are byte offsets relative to that function item's text.\n\nSignature/field/variant transformations preserve existing evaluation order and\nretained argument/value types in their supported cases. Missing reference,\nownership, constructor or scope evidence produces a located E_EDIT_* refusal.\nThe refusal is a request for an explicit source decision; replacing the complete\nauthored item is available when the independent checker can validate that change.\n\n--against asks the compiler to derive a request from a complete desired source\ntree and verify its checked meaning. For separate source roots, keep SOURCE and\nDESIRED_SOURCE relative and pass --source-dir and --against-source-dir separately.\nUse canonical absolute paths for both root selectors and their corresponding\n--library-dir and --against-library-dir roots. Each view uses its own library;\nsharing an old library between different source views can make include paths\nambiguous. Pass explicit editable library roots for library edits. --recover finishes\nor rolls back an interrupted publication; it takes no new request or target.\n\nQuery facts remain pinned to their old snapshot after publication. Build --index\nagain for a new query snapshot. See lkjscript query --help and compare --help.\n",
        "compare" => "lkjscript compare SOURCE --against REFERENCE_SOURCE [source/library options]\n                  [--against-source-dir ROOT] [--against-library-dir LIB]\n                  [--limit N] [--id ID]\n\nCheck both complete programs and compare their canonical checked meaning.\nFor distinct source roots:\n  lkjscript compare src/main.lkj --source-dir /absolute/candidate \\\n    --against src/main.lkj --against-source-dir /absolute/reference \\\n    --library-dir /absolute/candidate/library --against-library-dir /absolute/reference/library\n\nKeep each source path relative to its selected root. Use canonical absolute paths\nfor root and corresponding library selectors. Give each view its own library\ndirectory so library modules and included runtime source correspond.\n--limit bounds displayed changes; --id requests one identity's detail. The program's checked identities,\ndiagnostic metadata and source-declaration differences are labelled separately.\nA zero command exit means comparison completed; read the verdict to determine\nwhether canonical checked meaning is identical or differs. Canonical inequality\ndoes not itself prove a behavioral difference or an invalid candidate.\nThis command does not run tools/check.sh, native/interpreter test suites or CI.\n",
        _ => summary(),
    }
}
